  "releaseNotes": "# AID Studio v3.0.1\n\n## 中文\n\n### 新增\n\n- 全能画布助手支持将现有画布整理成可编辑的 Skill。保存并发布后，可从画布选择使用。\n- 支持管理个人录音，将录音绑定角色，并在画布视频和分镜视频中引用角色的声音。上传表单支持更换录音和头像，头像大小遵循站点的图片上传设置。\n\n- 升级和回退前自动备份服务端、管理后台、Web 和数据库。后台可设置备份目录和保留数量，默认保留最近一份。已有可用的当前版本备份时可直接切换，备份失败时会说明原因并停止升级或回退。\n- Docker 和手动部署可通过同一依赖包获取 FFmpeg 与升级器，按服务器架构取用。合包不可用时自动使用独立附件。\n- 全新安装会为仍使用初始口令的管理员生成随机密码，并保存到仅 root 可读的文件。无人值守部署可预设本地资源访问地址。\n- 分镜生图和自动宫格支持多张参考图，可从灵感空间选用角色、场景和道具。刷新后可恢复已提交的提示词和参考图。\n- 音画同步支持直接上传本地录音作为对口型素材，并在提交前显示报价。\n\n### 优化\n\n- 剧本流程和自由画布按创作入口显示模型。文本默认使用 DeepSeek V4.1 Flash，通用生图默认使用 GPT Image 2.6 Flare，视频默认使用 Seedance 2.5。高清放大、重绘、深度提取和标准配音使用各自的候选模型。\n- 低内存主机的 Web 构建会为编译进程留出更多空间。Docker 启动时会从网关检查应用服务的连通性。\n\n- Docker 安装按镜像并行检测公网下载源。按优先级发现可用源后立即拉取，失败时自动切换。FFmpeg 的独立下载优先从 AtomGit 获取，再尝试官方 CDN 和 GitHub。\n- 自动清理安装、构建和升级留下的临时文件，保留可复用的依赖缓存。本地存储的全新安装支持按选择自动导入官方资源包，失败后可继续使用系统并手动导入。\n- 后台将 Agent 和 Skill 分开编制，Skill 目录支持分页。相关业务页面可从同一导航入口进入。\n- 自由画布提示所选模型的输入条件和不兼容的参考素材。视频节点可定位报价失败的参考图，Skill 列表支持滚动加载并跟随主题。\n\n### 修复\n\n- 修复部分已安装站点升级时重复执行旧版 SQL，导致升级失败的问题。\n\n- 分镜图在同时设置清晰度和画幅时按所选比例生成。未指定时沿用项目画幅，成片按项目画幅导出。\n- 修复分镜生成完成后仍显示加载，以及自由画布整组执行无法运行组内图片节点的问题。\n- 修复 CentOS Stream 9 手动安装时受管 MySQL 的初始化问题。提交空部署配置会提示需要修改配置，避免无效重启。\n- 修复 Docker 新装时内置 MySQL 读不到初始化 SQL，以及旧版官方示例资源包在自动导入时无法通过文件校验的问题。\n\n### 升级注意事项\n\n- 从 2.2.4 升级前，请按 3.0.0 升级文档停服并整理旧版 Skill 标识，再继续升级。\n\n- MiniMax 语音合成与音色同步入口已下线。仍使用该渠道的角色请重新选择可用音色。已生成的音频、视频和历史账单仍可查看。\n\n- 自定义备份目录须提前创建，并允许升级器写入。恢复数据库会回到所选备份的时间点。\n- 旧配置的备份保留数为 3 时会调整为 1。需要继续保留 3 份时，可在升级后重新设置。\n\n## English\n\n### Added\n\n- Use the Canvas assistant to turn an existing canvas into a Skill. Edit and publish it, then select it from Canvas.\n- Manage personal recordings, assign them to characters, and reference character audio in Canvas and storyboard videos. Replace recordings and avatars in the upload form. Avatar size follows the site's image upload settings.\n\n- Upgrades and rollbacks back up the server, admin console, web application, and database. Administrators can set the backup directory and retention count. The system keeps the newest backup by default, reuses a valid backup when available, and stops the version change if backup fails.\n- Docker and manual installations can get FFmpeg and the updater from one runtime archive. The installer selects the files for the host architecture and falls back to separate downloads when needed.\n- Fresh installs generate a random password for the administrator account if it still uses the seed password. The installer saves it in a root-only file. Unattended installs can set the local resource origin in advance.\n- Storyboard generation and automatic grids accept multiple references from the inspiration library. Refreshing the page restores submitted prompts and references.\n- Lip-sync accepts local audio recordings and shows the estimated cost before submission.\n\n### Improved\n\n- Script-to-video and Canvas list models by creation feature. DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, GPT Image 2.6 Flare, and Seedance 2.5 are the defaults for text, general image generation, and video. Upscaling, inpainting, depth extraction, and voice generation have their own model choices.\n- Web builds leave more memory for compiler workers on smaller hosts. Docker startup checks that the gateway can reach the application services.\n\n- Docker installations probe public mirrors concurrently for each image and start pulling from the first eligible source in priority order. Standalone FFmpeg downloads use AtomGit first, then the official CDN and GitHub.\n- Installation and upgrade clean up temporary files and keep reusable dependency caches. Fresh installations with local storage can import the official assets automatically. If the import fails, AID remains available and the assets can be imported manually.\n- The admin console has separate Agent and Skill editors, a paginated Skill directory, and shared navigation for related pages.\n- Canvas explains model input requirements and incompatible references, highlights reference images that cause quote failures, and loads more Skills as users scroll.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Upgrades select SQL migrations after the installed version, including on sites without historical migration records.\n\n- Storyboard images honor the selected aspect ratio when a resolution is also set. Storyboards without an explicit aspect ratio use the project's aspect ratio, which also applies to episode exports.\n- Fixed the loading state after storyboard images complete and group execution for image nodes in Canvas.\n- Fixed managed MySQL initialization for manual installations on CentOS Stream 9. Submitting deployment settings with no changes now shows a message and avoids restarting services.\n- Fixed built-in MySQL initialization when Docker is installed with restrictive file permissions, and corrected file verification when automatically importing an older official asset archive.\n\n### Upgrade notes\n\n- If upgrading from 2.2.4, follow the 3.0.0 upgrade guide to stop the service and normalize legacy Skill identifiers first.\n\n- MiniMax speech synthesis and voice sync are retired. Choose another available voice for characters that used this provider. Existing generated media and billing records remain available.\n\n- Create the custom backup directory and grant the updater write access before upgrading. Restoring a database returns it to the time of the selected backup.\n- An existing retention count of 3 changes to 1. Set it back to 3 after upgrading if you want to keep three backups.",
